<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">United States Navy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1775">1775</a>–</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a> · Also known as US Navy</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/united-states">United States</a> Navy is the naval service of the United States, founded as the Continental Navy in 1775 and re-established under the Naval Act of 1794. In the 19th century its African Squadron patrolled the West African coast to suppress the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/atlantic-slave-trade">Atlantic slave trade</a>, and Africans freed from captured slave ships were landed in Liberia. It later became the world's largest navy and was decisive in the Pacific in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/second-world-war">Second World War</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-states-navy.jpg" alt="United States Navy" width="320" height="321" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Navy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Emblem_of_the_United_States_Navy.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
